2. Forge (coding) → New LLM session spawned with Di realm caps
3. Judge (testing) → New LLM session with Tian realm caps

The TUI Main Window persists; the Audience changes; the Edict remains constant in the banner until **Quenched** or **Rejected**.

### Shared Memory Avoidance
The LLM Session goroutine **never touches the TUI model directly**. It writes to `audience.Scrollback` (channel). The Bubble Tea `Update()` loop (main thread) pulls from this channel:

